            <div xml:id="d491">

                <pb facs="0720" n="638" sameAs="frus:frus1925v02/pg638"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00/3317: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Eberhardt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-09-21T11:00:00-05:45"><hi rendition="#italic">September 21,
                                1925—11 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 4:50
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>145. War vessels withdrew last night. There is no doubt that their presence
                    extricated President Solorzano from a difficult position and stopped temporarily
                    at least the tendency toward anarchy and revolution already commenced by
                    marauding bands.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Eberhardt</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
